A||N||8||GT-maniac||Battery Protection||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||07-07-2000||01:16 AM||||Has anyone figured out a way to protect the battery from the elements ? My car wouldn't start the other day because the terminals were wet from the torrential downpours we've had here recently. I'm also thinking I'm going to have to do something to protect it in the winter from the snow.<BR>I'm thinking maybe just cover the half of the grill that sits over top of the battery.<BR>I've got to do something as I'm not going to put with it not wanting to start every time it rains hard.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||07-07-2000||02:01 AM||||Clean and tighten the connections- smear them good with dialectric grease- I made a top cover out of a large plastic bottle that keeps rain and crap off .||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||07-07-2000||02:38 AM||||One popular solution, which helps with handling and engine cooling as well.. is to relocate the battery to the front compartment. This puts a bit more weight over the front wheels, as well as allowing more open space for air to flow out of the decklid vents.. and when it's in the front compartment, it's a bit easier to protect from the elements.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-07-2000||10:10 AM||||Will '84 covers fit on later cars?  I plan on getting Toms scoop so cooling might not be a problem with the vents closed off.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||07-07-2000||04:41 PM||||I think the 84 covers are awfull looking.<P>I just keep my terminals tight and greased. Dielectric grease is prefered but anything that will repell water works.<P>anything that's a heavy UV resistant plastic will work to make a battery cover. A sheet of truck innner tube rubber works just fine too. just tuck it in between the front of the battery and the tray and let it drape over the top and terminals.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-08-2000||09:24 AM||||Mr. Ogre--I was thinking about getting Toms rear scoop, then installing a pair of '84 covers and painting them to match the car (pearlized purple).  What do you find ugly about them.  I haven't seen many up close.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||07-08-2000||12:04 PM||||painted to match they might no be bad. OEM black looks bad even on the black cars. Plus they are completely flat. no contour at all. They might not line up right allong the back endge. Remember the 84 lid is flat too. not like the 85 + lids.<P>I'd paint both sets to match and see how they look. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||07-08-2000||12:05 PM||||painted to match they might no be bad. OEM black looks bad even on the black cars. Plus they are completely flat. no contour at all. They might not line up right allong the back endge. Remember the 84 lid is flat too. not like the 85 + lids.<P>I'd paint both sets to match and see how they look.<P>I found for my black car, I like the semi gloss paints for mirrors and grates. You take the screen off the bottom and paint it silver. It looks nice. Especially the old hex hole screen, the slot screen looks awful no mater what you do to it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT-maniac||07-08-2000||10:21 PM||||I like the plastic cover idea and the inner tube should work too. Relocating the battery sound a bit more involved than I have time for at the moment.<BR>On the topic of the grille covers I'd have to agree the 84 covers are awfull, I don't much care for the el cheapo stamped tin covers I've seen on the later fieros either.<BR>I much prefer the heavy pot metal covers on my 85. Of course I may be a little biased there :^)<P>Thanks for the replies everybody and if you have any ideas screwed up shifter please feel free..<P>BTW Ogre what the adress of your web page ?||||reg||1
